1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,569
On Q-Day, nobody has to steal your password.

2
00:00:03,889 --> 00:00:07,624
A quantum computer can work out your private key from your public one.

3
00:00:07,944 --> 00:00:09,302
So QoreChain ran a drill.

4
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:13,077
On 18 November, a bot got the classical key of our drill account,

5
00:00:13,077 --> 00:00:15,682
and it had a whole day to take whatever it could.

6
00:00:16,582 --> 00:00:20,448
This is Kavach Vault. It holds an AI agent's money on QoreChain.

7
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:22,941
The agent can ask to pay someone,

8
00:00:22,941 --> 00:00:28,406
but nothing leaves the vault without a signature from the owner's post-quantum key,

9
00:00:28,406 --> 00:00:30,250
ML-DSA-87, checked on chain.

10
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:33,015
Who sends the transaction doesn't matter.

11
00:00:33,015 --> 00:00:35,638
The vault never trusts the caller's address.

12
00:00:36,938 --> 00:00:37,983
We split the money.

13
00:00:38,303 --> 00:00:43,057
85% sits in a cold vault that can't move before 20 November.

14
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:48,455
The rest is in a hot vault, with a cap per payment, a daily cap, an allowlist,

15
00:00:48,455 --> 00:00:51,841
a 6-hour timelock, and a guardian who can freeze it.

16
00:00:52,161 --> 00:00:55,234
The drill account never opens an EVM window.

17
00:00:55,234 --> 00:00:59,005
It holds 1 test QOR that its classical key can't move.

18
00:00:59,325 --> 00:01:03,113
Even our own fees come from a fee grant, so its balance never drops.

19
00:01:04,013 --> 00:01:07,931
Before the drill, we attacked ourselves with the real leaked key.

20
00:01:08,251 --> 00:01:13,658
298 native transactions, covering every message type in the SDK.

21
00:01:13,978 --> 00:01:18,366
34 EVM transactions. 78 drain calls on the vaults.

22
00:01:18,686 --> 00:01:20,044
Not one got through.

23
00:01:21,544 --> 00:01:26,821
Then the drill. One minute after midnight UTC, our proof of life landed.

24
00:01:27,141 --> 00:01:31,012
It's not a transfer to ourselves. It's a real vault action:

25
00:01:31,012 --> 00:01:32,914
the owner's signed heartbeat.

26
00:01:33,234 --> 00:01:36,828
All day, a watchtower read the chain every 15 seconds,

27
00:01:36,828 --> 00:01:39,556
ready to freeze the hot vault on its own.

28
00:01:39,876 --> 00:01:41,029
We'd tested that.

29
00:01:41,029 --> 00:01:45,571
An unauthorised withdrawal on a test vault was frozen in 6 seconds.

30
00:01:45,891 --> 00:01:48,448
And so the drill didn't hang on one laptop,

31
00:01:48,448 --> 00:01:53,205
a keyless backup on GitHub Actions and Vercel held only pre-signed transactions.

32
00:01:53,525 --> 00:01:54,522
While building it,

33
00:01:54,522 --> 00:01:57,847
we found that someone could block it by copying a signature.

34
00:01:57,847 --> 00:01:59,011
So we fixed that too.

35
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:04,099
When the day ended, the drill account had started with 1 QOR,

36
00:02:04,099 --> 00:02:05,266
and ended with 1.

37
00:02:05,586 --> 00:02:10,706
100% kept. Both vaults untouched. Not one alarm.

38
00:02:11,026 --> 00:02:13,807
We pushed our predictions to GitHub during the drill,

39
00:02:13,807 --> 00:02:17,165
before the attack log was out, so you can check us line by line.

40
00:02:18,865 --> 00:02:24,747
Underneath: 94 Foundry tests, 6 invariants, fuzzing, symbolic checks,

41
00:02:24,747 --> 00:02:26,963
and all 27 mutants killed.

42
00:02:27,283 --> 00:02:29,642
Every claim links to its proof in the repo,

43
00:02:29,642 --> 00:02:32,220
with commands to check the live chain yourself.

44
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:36,040
Kavach Vault. A stolen classical key moves nothing.
